.TH QUANT-LSP 1 "July 2026" "Quant 1.0.0" "Quant Language Tools"
.SH NAME
quant\-lsp \- Language Server Protocol server for Quant
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quant\-lsp
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B quant\-lsp
implements the Language Server Protocol for the Quant language.
It communicates over stdin/stdout using JSON-RPC and is intended to be
launched automatically by an LSP-capable editor such as VS Code, Neovim,
or Emacs.
.PP
The server performs full incremental analysis on every file save, providing
diagnostics, completions, hover information, and more without requiring a
separate build step.
.SH PROTOCOL FEATURES
.TP
.B Diagnostics
Type errors and undefined references reported on every save.
.TP
.B Hover
Type signature and doc comment of the symbol under the cursor.
.TP
.B Completion
Context-aware completion for local variables, functions, struct fields,
and standard library names.
.TP
.B Go to definition
Jump to the declaration of any function or variable.
.TP
.B Go to type definition
Jump to the struct or error-set declaration for a typed expression.
.TP
.B Find references / Rename
Locate and rename all uses of a function or variable across open files.
.TP
.B Document symbols / Workspace symbols
Outline of all functions and structs; fuzzy search across the workspace.
.TP
.B Signature help
Parameter list and current-argument highlight while typing a call.
.TP
.B Semantic tokens
Full-file syntax highlighting driven by the type-checked AST.
.TP
.B Inlay hints
Inferred types shown after variable declarations; parameter names at call
sites.
.TP
.B Code actions
Quick fixes: add missing import, fill missing struct fields.
.TP
.B Code lens
Reference count displayed above every function declaration.
.TP
.B Call hierarchy
Incoming and outgoing call trees for any function.
.TP
.B Folding ranges
Collapse blocks, functions, and import groups.
.TP
.B Selection range
Smart expand-selection from identifier to expression to block to function.
.TP
.B Formatting
Whole-document format via \fBquant\-fmt\fR, comment-preserving and idempotent.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QUANT_STDLIB
Path to the Quant standard library. The LSP uses this to resolve imports
when analysing open files.
.SH NOTES
.B quant\-lsp
is ordinarily started by the editor, not the user. For VS Code, install
the Quant LSP extension; it will launch and restart
.B quant\-lsp
automatically.
.PP
For other editors, configure the LSP client to run \fBquant\-lsp\fR with
no arguments; communication is over stdin/stdout.
